  "summary": "Phase 1b of the occurrence-host plan moved typed-text recognition and preedit text into public Plite calls, in the working tree; Phases 2 and 3 have not run. Plite reports text a mounted Editable committed with typing intent through api.react.subscribeTypedText, naming the text just before the commit's caret, and reads the DOM text before the caret through api.dom.textToCaret. Android's pending diffs keep their input type, the input-event fallback reports its Editable, a DOM repair that leaves the caret elsewhere opens no typing scope, and a commit whose document an earlier listener changed reports nothing. Plate's combobox owner opens an occurrence only from a report for its own Editable and stops reading Plite's private tags and placeholder characters. Phase 1b adds no Android flush, so a merged diff of typed and pasted text reports nothing. The api-build panel ran four rounds, two past its cap, and the round-5 patch shipped unreviewed on the owner's word.",
